Negative control for the transport returning the criteria to BOOT STATE — on
`stop`, on `arm`, and on every backward `seek` (T4.2 · AC2.6 · §3.1 ruling 1).

The port's `set` merges at BRANCH level: `set({ filters })` replaces the whole
`filters` branch and leaves `sort` and `pagination` standing, and a payload that
does not NAME a branch leaves that branch exactly as it was. An unfiltered boot
model carries no `filters` branch at all — `useQueryCriteria`'s model is the
parsed intent with empty containers compacted away — so handing the boot state
back on its own can never unwind a filter a scene applied. It merges into it.

This mutant is that omission, and nothing else: the reset still fires at every
site it fires at today, still clones, still writes through the port's own `set`.
It simply stops naming the branches the boot state does not carry.

What it looks like when it is live, and what no shape assertion catches: Stop
returns the BAR to Live and clears `track=`/`scene=` while the page stays
filtered to a state the user never chose (`filter.verified.eq=false` surviving in
the url, "showing 0 of 0" on screen); and a backward seek rewinds the playhead,
the marked step and the Code pane while the SURFACE keeps the rows the forward
pass narrowed it to. Every transport-state assertion stays green throughout —
the playhead, the status, the url and the arm order are all correct. Only the
criteria are wrong.

Apply from the repo root: `git apply <this file>`; revert with `git apply -R`.

Reds: the T4.2 cases asserting the criteria are back at boot state — but ONLY
against a boot model of the shape the composable actually publishes. A fixture
whose boot state already NAMES every branch a scene writes (`{ filters: {} }`)
passes under this mutant and under the fix alike, because naming the branch is
the whole of what is missing: the merge replaces it either way. The proving case
must therefore boot from a model that does NOT carry the branch the scene adds
— boot `{ sort, pagination }`, scene `set({ filters: … })` — and assert on
`criteria.model.value` after `stop()` and after a backward `seek()`.

  Proven RED: owed by the prover's blind run (`vitest run --project unit
  scenario-player`). Recorded here rather than pre-filled, because the assertion
  this control exists to catch is the one the fix is being proven by, and the
  seat that authors the mutant is not the seat that grades it.

